hello everyone my name is harini  balasubramanian and i'm a research  fellow at pine biotech today i will be  presenting my project titled in silico  comparative transcriptomic analysis of  endemic and epidemic kubose sarcoma  this project was mentored by dr  raghavendran lakshmi narayan  before i begin into  the details about my project i would  like to tell you a little bit about  myself  so  my uh  i have a bachelor's degree in industrial  biotechnology from anna university india  my research interests predominantly lie  in  molecular biology so some example areas  are micro rna profile analysis  toxicogenomics precision medicine cancer  biology and methylation epigenetics  i aspired to pursue my master's degree  in molecular and cellular biology  so  what is capocity sarcoma  kaposi sarcoma is an anti-proliferative  multicentric malignancy that is  triggered by the infection of kshv or  kaposi sarcoma associated herpes virus  it has four distinct clinical subtypes  first epidemic ks which is an aggressive  subtype that is commonly occurring in  hiv zero positive individuals second  the classic chaos which is found in  older men of eastern european descent  third in the michaels which is prevalent  in certain areas of equatorial or  sub-saharan africa  and lastly  transplant-related ks which occurs when  an immunosuppressed transplant patient  is also infected with kshp  so kshv is an oncogenic human gamma  herpes virus  which is also the etiological agent that  is responsible for not only kaposi  sarcoma but also strongly associated  with b-cell proliferative disorders  including primary effusion lymphoma  the variant binds to the cell surface  receptor following which the viral dna  migrates into the nucleus  kshv exists between a lytic and latent  life cycle upon infection kshv  establishes a long-term persistent  infection in humans where it manipulates  multiple host signaling pathways and  also modulates the expression of  cellular genes to thrive in the infected  cells  in general kshv infection is essential  but not adequate to induce ks disease  progression  despite antiretroviral treatment the  prognosis for ks is often poor with high  mortality due to the presentation of  late cancer stage  therefore  to identify more accurate detection  methods and therapeutic targets against  ks a better understanding of the viral  and trans and cellular transcriptomes in  the cancer are necessary  so  this is the information about the data  set that i obtained for my analysis the  data was downloaded from the nc ncbi geo  platform in raw rate counts  the study involved a total of 51 samples  of which three samples of normal skin  were taken from three healthy  individuals and the rest from ks  patients  here the samples from the diseased  individuals were obtained in pairs that  is the biopsies from lesional skin and  uninvolved sites on the same individual  were collected  raw cons for each chain from the human  and kshv transcriptomes were provided by  the authors  this is the methodology and the  flowchart that i followed for the for my  analysis  uh firstly i group the samples into  endemic care samples epidemic and normal  skin  secondly uh exploratory analysis or  principal component analysis here was  conducted using the the following  parameters  pca was conducted first for all the  samples and then for endemic and  epidemic separately  next differential expression analysis  using the desector algorithm and the  enrichment and gse modules were also  performed  to understand the upregulated and  downregulated genes  and these were the parameters that were  used for the analysis  and lastly human gage analysis for a  better understanding of the pathways was  also performed using the parameters as  given on the flow chart  these are the results of the pca  pipeline  and  this is the result for the  uh differential expression and human  gene uh human gauge results so  um for epidemic ks and endemic ks uh dot  plots for geoengi pathways  seen at plots also for enriched pathways  volcano plots uh they were all obtained  and uh for epidemic case alone the  arachidonic acid pathway and retinol  metabolism were significantly  downregulated  similarly for endemic ks  the human gauge results showed that the  ribosome pathway was also significantly  suppressed  now moving on to the biological  interpretation part of the results that  we've obtained from our pipelines  so a majorly upregulated gene in endemic  ks was sox11 so sox11 is a neural  transcription factors which is highly  expressed in mesenchymal and neural  progenitor cells  it is also considered an oncogene  because of its ability to induce  tumorogenesis by promoting cell survival  so the increased transcript level of  this gene can be implicated  in  can be implicated in  the progression of the cancer and it can  be an important biomarker of capocity  sarcoma provide  sorry provided that the detection assay  is also coupled with certain viral genes  and  in endemic in epidemic ks the orf6 viral  gene was most upregulated and this was  restricted only to epidemic years  it is a gene that is activated during  early lighting replication phase in  age-related ks  so co-infection with hiv in aids rated  ks  accelerates and aggravates  chaos development so it is possible that  the high levels of the gene product were  also a result of the indirect role of  hiv in disease propagation  next let's move on to the results of the  volcano plot for epidemic years  so ppf ppe f1 and pcdh17  along with cemip  were found to be massively upregulated  so ppef1  is significantly correlated with retinal  degeneration and pcdh17 and cemip were  found to uh have positive  correlations with cell to cell  connection and epithelial mesenchymal  transition pathways  so the over expression of these genes in  uh  epidemic is patients is indicative of  sarcoma progression  next let's look at the volcano plot for  endemic ks  so first uh  if we see the uh  s100 a1 gene  it plays an important role in inhibition  of microtubule assembly so its increased  transcription level can be implicated in  promoting cell proliferation and  migration like the pc  sk16 and thereby the metastasis of  cancer cancer tissues  moving on to the pathways  the lipid metabolism and energy the  energy generation pathways  were significantly downregulated in  epidemic years  the lack of regulation in lipid  metabolism was observed in both  subtypes  but the transcriptional imbalance was  more pronounced in  epidemic yes  and this can be seen in the arachidonic  acid pathway as i mentioned earlier  the arachidonic acid is a multifaceted  pufa molecule that uh confers cell  permeability that confirms permeability  to the cell membrane and also produces  uh is also involved in producing  prostaglandins and leukotrienes  so ara or arachidonic acid oxidation  produces many other crucial molecules  that participate in wound healing energy  balance and response to pathogen  invasion  so the suppression of this pathway in  epidemic es can be implicated in the  reduced immune response and dysfunction  of the central nervous system  next  another down regulated pathway in  epidemic ks was the retinol metabolism  pathway  so retinas are known to inhibit  uncontrolled cell growth and  the the suppression of this pathway  substantiates the significant anti-tumor  efficacy of the current use of retinoids  in treating localized skin lesions  and lastly the ribosomal proteins  pathway uh was  suppressed in the endemic case  samples  so  this may be connected to the recent  fascinating discovery that kshv induces  production of the specific ribosomes  that are preferential for viral lactic  phase mrnas so it's possible that the  virus manipulates the cell machinery to  suppress the organically produced  ribosomes in favor of the ribosomal  proteins that aid in viral lytic protein  production  in conclusion  six genes in endemic years and epidemic  yes were identified respectively to be  differentially expressed in these  disease conditions  while the incidence of endemic ks is  decreasing in developed countries like  the usa it is still very prevalent in  sub-saharan africa and the mediterranean  so  till date the detection of lana or  the orf-1 gene product is the golden  standard for kshv diagnostics in this  study too orf73 gene uh which encodes  for lana um  was found to be well upregulated in both  conditions with similar fall change  values  but how far a lana-based assay can  characterize the extent of case  progression is not clear  so from our from this study uh two two  potential biomarkers have been  identified one orf6 and two sox11  uh orf6  uh could be a potential biomarker for  detecting co-infection in kshv in  hiv-positive individuals  and sox-11 since it's heavily involved  in propagating lesions and triggering  angiogenesis makes it another uh  prospective biomarker for ks  so in conclusion more research on the  physiological and genotypic presentation  of capocity sarcoma is highly essential  to discover more therapeutic targets  that can increase not only the longevity  but also the quality of life in people  living with hiv and in ks patients  these are the references that i used  thank you so much
 

